WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:08.320
<b>The 
angels</b>

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:08.320
<b>shall 
bring</b>

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:08.320
<b>true death
 upon the 
performers.
 — V</b>

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.210
<i>This is Kanagawa Traffic Police Unit 205.</i>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.160
<i>Arrest made at scene. Middle-aged male;
 requesting identity check.</i>

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.650
Mister Officer, are we there yet?

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.740
Almost.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.730
That was impressive, though.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.250
You're literally a little detective.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.680
You and the bodyguard would 
make an excellent detective duo.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:31.270
I don't think that guy has any 
interest in working with me, though.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:33.720
Oh, is that so?

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.230
That guy's afraid of strangers.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.790
You've only just met him, 
yet you know him so well.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.600
You truly are gifted.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.690
You have the ability to see 
through the truth, don't you?

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.140
Though...

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.940
You don't actually believe that, do you?

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:58.480
I mean, you said I've only just met him.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.800
That means you just checked 
in with headquarters

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.800
and found out that I only met Fukuzawa-san 
after the president's assassination.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.420
You wanted to test my ability.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.290
Impressive.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.200
Shucks, I really underestimated you.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:17.440
I hate that you're still doubting me.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.210
Want me to prove that I'm Gifted?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.760
What an honor!

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:26.180
I get a front-row seat to a 
Gifted detective at work.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.090
This car isn't headed to 
the police station, is it?

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.710
I should have told you sooner.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:34.780
I'm sorry.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.420
I received a dispatch just before we left.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.770
There's been an incident,

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.590
and they want me to take the 
expert detective there.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.750
I see.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:48.650
But I don't think you needed to use your 
special ability to figure that out.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.080
The police station is 
towards the train station.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.740
It doesn't take much to realize 
we're going the wrong way.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.450
Let's do this, then.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:59.920
You can ask me anything 
about the last incident.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:03.460
If I can't answer your question, you win.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.490
If you run out of questions, I win.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:06.790
How's that?

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:07.950
Makes sense.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.210
Okay, here's a question
 I'm sure is on everyone's mind:

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:15.360
You know the gentleman in the 
suit who was arrested on stage?

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:19.780
How do you think he was 
captured and taken there?

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:21.870
A rug.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:23.370
A rug?

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.880
You remember the high-pile rugs in the hall?

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.840
One of them was missing 
after the whole panic.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.840
Also, there was a faint odor 
 where the rug was.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.170
It's like...

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:42.050
That weird-smelling stuff they use 
to make paint and plastics and stuff.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.600
Organic solvent?

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:44.730
Yeah! That's it!

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.060
I caught a whiff of the same smell 
from that gentleman in the suit.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:54.950
Which means the attacker must have wrapped 
him up in the rug and taken him there.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.600
The attacker used the organic 
solvent to knock him out first.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.350
There was certainly a lot of commotion,
 with actors and municipal police at the scene.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:11.440
A man moving a rug around might not 
have drawn that much attention.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.320
Still, we're certain that it was 
the accomplice, the stagewright,

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.240
who moved the man. Correct?

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.980
It wasn't the stagewright.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:25.320
I think he was probably murdered 
before the performance.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:30.470
Everyone else besides me is thoroughly 
stupid and foolish and worthy of compassion.

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:33.250
So I wish I could have saved him,

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:37.110
but there isn't much I can do for someone 
who's been dead since before the case.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:42.110
Why would they do all that just 
to abduct one person, though?

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.210
An abduction?

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:53.060
The whole project was a elaborate trap set up
 just to abduct the gentleman in the suit.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:58.870
The stagewright and the main star, 
Murakami-san, were just pawns to that end.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.280
Well?

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.880
Now do you believe I'm Gifted?

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.080
So come on...

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.520
Just tell me where this car's going already.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:15.560
Well, Mister So-Called Officer, 
who smells of organic solvent?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.340
Why can't you get in touch with them?

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.650
We still don't have confirmation that
 they arrived at the station yet.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:57.290
Nor can we connect to the 
police radio in the vehicle.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.170
<i>The stagewright was murdered.</i>

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:11.540
<i>Judging from what Rampo told
 Egawa Joshi, this case isn't over yet.</i>

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:16.500
This crime is comprised of 
two different kinds of acts.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.570
You could think of it like 
a shrimp and a sea bream.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.070
<i>The real perpetrator is still on the loose.</i>

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.200
You could be satisfied with the shrimp,
 which is easy to catch.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.990
<i>He must be talking about 
the actor, Murakami.</i>

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.840
But if you want to catch the sea bream,

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.820
well, you're going to 
have to use the shrimp.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.830
<i>So the true perpetrator is plotting an even
 larger crime using the actor, Murakami,</i>

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.170
<i>and the stagewright, Kurahashi.</i>

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:44.080
<i>Rampo is intent on
 exposing that perpetrator.</i>

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.560
What's the name of the officer who 
went to the station with Rampo?

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.290
Senior Officer Mitamura.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:52.380
His phone's been switched off, as well.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:57.970
<i>What's happened to Rampo?</i>

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.470
<i>Where is Rampo?</i>

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.290
<b>Fukuzawa 
Yukichi</b>

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.870
See ya later!

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:33.090
That must be when...

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:39.430
<b>The perpetrator
 is Mitamura</b>

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:39.430
<b>Find the cane</b>

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.430
Unbelievable... Truly unbelievable!

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:46.440
To think we didn't have such an 
exceptional Gifted on our research list...

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:50.380
Officially, this place is an office 
for a shipbuilding firm.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:53.410
It's what you'd call a shell company.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.170
Anyway, have a seat.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.610
A gun, huh?

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.620
Oh.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.300
I have no intention of using it...

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.460
As long as you do as I say.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:24.930
That's the cane!

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:32.920
A concealed weapon.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:44.870
Damn...

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.380
That gentleman!

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.650
<i>Have you changed your mind?</i>

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:03.070
I have a request.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.190
Well?

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:08.860
Where are we?

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:13.560
Like I said, it's one of 
our convenient outposts.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:15.350
"Our"?

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:18.010
I don't mean the 
municipal police, of course.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:23.890
Four career soldiers with guns on guard.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:25.690
No...

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:27.930
There are five.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.080
Magnificent!

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.680
How did you know?

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.990
Because that's my special ability.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:39.290
They don't have the slightest 
intention of harming you, though.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:46.980
Those men were prepared to keep 
an eye on the original target—

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.690
the gentleman you 
revealed on the stage.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:54.060
And the gentleman got away.

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:57.750
So, why did you bring me here?

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:01.470
The plot at the theater 
was pretty elaborate.

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:05.300
The brass is furious that their 
investment's been ruined.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.380
They're insisting that I catch the 
guy who messed everything up.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.560
Make him explain how he 
saw through the scheme.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.760
Where he got the information.

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:23.550
Otherwise, we'll be forced to follow our 
orders to hurt you, though we disagree.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:25.010
You wouldn't want that, would you?

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.810
So I have a proposal for you, 
Mister Gifted Detective...

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:33.300
Would you like to work with us?

00:10:34.180 --> 00:10:36.660
We have a vision.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:40.340
To rid this country of evil people.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:45.910
An excellent Gifted such as yourself 
would be more than welcome.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:47.550
What do you think?

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.620
Oh, sorry,

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.500
I got bored of your long rambling.

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:56.060
I wasn't listening at all.

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.110
How do you like your cell?

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:05.580
Not bad.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.190
There's air conditioning.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.690
I told them I was bored, 
and they gave me this.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:13.140
I guess they're telling me to repent.

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:15.820
I'm here with a question.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:18.160
Look at this.

00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:22.630
This is a memory device employed 
by a certain government agency.

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:26.340
It's a device used by those 
under witness protection

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:29.180
to communicate with the protection agency.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:33.600
Only high-priority people being targeted 
by criminal organizations would have one.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:38.410
Such people all have one thing in common:

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.970
They're all Gifted.

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:46.870
I'm sure someone as capable as you would 
have taken external clients, as well.

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.870
Have you accepted any requests 
to capture a Gifted recently?

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.950
I can't talk about my clients.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.650
It doesn't have to have been a client.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:12:02.180
Have you heard anything recently 
about capturing a Gifted alive?

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:06.950
The request may have come from 
someone who calls themselves V.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.210
I don't want to talk about them.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:16.090
Do you know what their objective is?

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:17.030
No.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:18.040
It's a ritual.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.990
Killing for money, killing out of spite...

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:25.000
Those things make sense to me.

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:28.790
But to them, the killing is the ritual.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.270
I don't want to get involved 
with those types.

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:39.250
If you're killing as a ritual, 
it doesn't matter who you kill.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.320
That's where you ultimately end up.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:59.870
I'm not ordering you to fight them.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:03.180
An acquaintance of mine 
has been abducted by them.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.850
Do you know where they might be holding him?

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.080
I have no reason to tell you.

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.210
You're absolutely right.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.200
But if you do tell me,

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:20.260
I'll testify that you fired in self-defense 
and killed him by accident.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.760
They'll let you out immediately.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.440
I'm surprised.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:41.090
You don't look like the kind of person 
who would sell out on justice like that.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:44.070
<i>I didn't think I was, either.</i>

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:49.350
I've always worked as a killer on my own.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:53.460
I've never wanted any 
coworkers or superiors.

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:57.090
But if a skilled martial 
artist such as yourself

00:13:57.090 --> 00:14:00.150
would go against your principles 
just to save your subordinate...

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.700
He's lucky to have you.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.650
I envy him a little.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:06.750
No.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.780
<i>He isn't a subordinate.</i>

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:13.720
I've heard about several buildings 
they use for their dealings.

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:17.100
Do we have an agreement?

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.750
I could escape at any point if I wanted to.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.240
The reward you're promising 
isn't quite worth it.

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:28.000
But the food at this facility is awful.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:33.000
If you happen to have some sway here, 
would you mind talking to them?

00:14:33.490 --> 00:14:35.030
Any requests?

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:40.290
Curry rice.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.790
Listen up, great detective.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:51.350
Our organization is formidable and flawless.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:57.430
I think it would be far more rewarding than 
teaming up with that bodyguard.

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:58.900
Moo.

00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:04.190
I can't pay attention to things 
I have no interest in.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:06.790
It just sounds like cattle mooing to me.

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:07.980
Moo!

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.550
Moo!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:13.420
You're extremely fortunate that
 I'm the one you're negotiating with.

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:18.300
Anyone else might have started sawing you 
apart from your nails upward by now.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:19.650
He's mooing again.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:20.680
Moo!

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:22.020
Moo!

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:26.500
Looks like we need to use this to 
move the conversation forward.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:31.210
You can use your gift to see 
through the truth. So what?

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:34.280
You're too feeble to stop a single bullet.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:40.760
I only gave you my time for the 
sake of our grand objective.

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:45.990
We'll wipe out all the Gifted 
rotting this country's foundations.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.600
I see.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:52.500
V is an organization of Gifted 
brought together to drive out Gifted.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.150
Oh, wait, gimme a sec.

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:00.890
By my predictions,

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.220
you have three seconds.

00:16:03.570 --> 00:16:04.310
Two.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:06.820
One.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.000
I took out one of the guards outside.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:17.740
How many more are there?

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:20.280
Four.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.150
One more.

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:49.520
Freaks!

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:07.710
Are you all right?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:08.850
Yeah!

00:17:10.240 --> 00:17:12.980
Wow, that went better than I expected.

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:15.250
Although you arrived just in time,
 just as I calculated.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:28.650
Screw you!

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.980
To hell with your damn calculations!

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:35.650
When I got here, I saw a 
gun pointed at your face.

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.010
That was only because I knew you would come!

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:40.070
Showing off your abilities is fine.

00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:43.780
And using your intellect to 
face powerful enemies is good.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:49.120
But stop wagering your own 
life on your gambles!

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.570
You're still a child.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:04.860
I'm sorry.

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:07.060
I'm sorry.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.520
I'm sorry.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:10.560
I'm sorry.

00:18:11.010 --> 00:18:12.190
I'm sorry.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:13.430
I'm sorry.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:14.740
I'm sorry.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:15.720
I'm sorry.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:16.490
I'm sorry.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:17.620
I'm sorry.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:19.430
I'm sorry.

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:20.780
I'm sorry.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:21.990
I'm sorry.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:37.640
Officer Mitamura was 
murdered while in custody.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.310
He's been silenced.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:43.700
So the plot continues.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:48.780
But who is the perpetrator 
of the last incident, V?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.730
It's not "V."

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:56.770
It's Five.

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:04.950
What is it?

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:12.460
I was just thinking, the cityscape looks 
different somehow, compared to yesterday.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:14.540
Why do you think?

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:17.010
Because you understand now.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.210
That I'm Gifted?

00:19:21.440 --> 00:19:22.770
Not that.

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:26.480
You understand what's important.

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.490
Curry...

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.170
So spicy!

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:42.050
But so good.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.150
Is this it?

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:21.330
Should be.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:36.100
Welcome to Bankoudou.

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:40.110
Oh.

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:43.830
The cane I lost a while back.

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:47.620
I happened to hear about you,

00:21:47.620 --> 00:21:51.570
so I took the liberty of coming 
to discuss your proposal.

00:21:52.130 --> 00:21:53.650
Don't be so formal about it.

00:21:54.270 --> 00:21:55.730
Have a seat.

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:56.490
Sir.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.430
No way...

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.220
I never noticed at the time, 
but is this man really so...

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:08.060
I owe you one, boy.

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:09.340
Right!

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:13.080
You saw through the trap from 
the beginning of the play,

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:16.160
and you let capture you anyway.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:20.350
You flushed out the enemy 
so that we would catch them.

00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:24.770
Though the sea bream seems 
to have gotten away.

00:22:24.770 --> 00:22:26.780
I have come with a request.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:29.010
As I'm sure you're aware,

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:33.360
Edogawa Rampo here is building a reputation 
for himself as a Gifted detective,

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:39.120
but it's taboo for a Gifted 
to promote themselves publicly.

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:42.530
That's why I would like your help.

00:22:43.350 --> 00:22:46.400
A Gifted Business Permit. I see.

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:49.660
So you intend to start a business.

00:22:50.420 --> 00:22:51.140
Yes.

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:54.380
In order to obtain a permit

00:22:54.820 --> 00:22:59.870
from the Gifted Special Operations Division, 
I require your vast knowledge in that area.

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:02.220
Natsume Soseki, sir.

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:07.050
It won't be an easy path,

00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:12.520
but I think you can make it happen.

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:14.860
If anyone can, it will be you two.

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:20.290
For Fukuzawa and Rampo

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:26.840
this was when it all began.

